# Furrow configuration via environment variables
# This file is loaded automatically by pydantic-settings from .env (not tracked in git).
# Copy to .env and uncomment/edit values as needed. All lines are commented so copying is safe.
#
# Every commented line below carries a working example value, never a bare name:
# uncommenting `FURROW_MODEL=` would set it to the empty string, which is not the
# same as leaving it unset and would send an unnamed model to the provider. Edit
# the value on the right-hand side; do not delete it.

# LLM provider: anthropic | openai | ollama (default: anthropic)
# FURROW_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Default model used when no role-specific model is set
# FURROW_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# Role-specific models (override the default model for that role)
# FURROW_PLANNER_MODEL=claude-3-5-haiku-20241022
# FURROW_WORKER_MODEL=claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022
# FURROW_TESTER_MODEL=claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022

# Override model that wins over all four role models above; leave commented to let
# each role use its own model. Must match the provider you selected.
# FURROW_OVERRIDE_MODEL=claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022

# API keys (FURROW_* take precedence; plain ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OPENAI_API_KEY used as fallback).
# Replace the placeholder with a real key from the provider's console.
# FURROW_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-replace-with-your-key
# FURROW_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-replace-with-your-key

# Ollama base URL (default: http://localhost:11434); only read by provider=ollama
# FURROW_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434

# Execution limits
# FURROW_MAX_PARALLEL_TASKS=5
# FURROW_MAX_CYCLES=0
# FURROW_MAX_TOKENS=4096
# FURROW_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=120.0
# FURROW_MAX_RETRIES=3

# Test settings: FURROW_TEST_COMMAND overrides auto-detection, which probes
# `pytest -q`, `python -m pytest -q`, `npm test`, `pnpm test`, `yarn test`,
# `cargo test -q` and `go test ./...` in that order.
# FURROW_TEST_TIMEOUT=120.0
# FURROW_TEST_COMMAND=pytest -q

# Workspace root (default: current working directory); every file the agent
# touches is resolved inside it.
# FURROW_WORKSPACE=.

# Logging level: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL (case-insensitive)
# Applied to the root logger by `furrow start` and `furrow web`; CRITICAL is
# quieter than ERROR. An unrecognised value is a configuration error.
# FURROW_LOG_LEVEL=INFO